OWNERSHIP AND SCOPE

Copyright is held by Pryor Consulting.

The governing agreement between St. John Fisher University and Pryor Consulting
for the Academic Catalog AI Ecosystem project defines its deliverables as a set
of modular AI bots, together with supporting documentation and training
materials. Its assignment clause — under which work product becomes client
property upon final payment — reaches that commissioned work product.

The platform in this repository is broader than those deliverables. The web
application, the verification harness, the ingestion pipeline, the spoke
generator, and the database schema were not commissioned under that agreement.
They are Pryor Consulting's own work, and they are provided to St. John Fisher
University for its use as a grant beyond the agreed scope rather than by
assignment.

Separately, final payment for the final submission of the work has not been
made, so the assignment condition has not been satisfied in any case.

ST. JOHN FISHER UNIVERSITY'S RIGHTS

St. John Fisher University may use, operate, modify, and maintain this system
for its own institutional purposes, including after the transfer of hosting
accounts and credentials described in TRANSFER_RUNBOOK.md. This grant is not
exclusive and does not transfer copyright.

RETAINED RIGHTS

Pryor Consulting retains all rights in the general machinery — including the
verification harness, the ingestion pipeline, the spoke generator, and the
application framework — and may reuse it in future engagements of a
conceptually similar kind.

Any such reuse must be de-identified: no St. John Fisher University name, brand,
domain, project reference, bucket name, deployment URL, tenant identifier, or
catalog content may appear in a derived work for another institution. This is the
same rule stated in CLAUDE.md section 5, applied in the outbound direction.

Client-specific material is excluded from that reuse right: catalog data,
branding, institutional configuration, and content authored by or for the
university.

See docs/IP_AND_OWNERSHIP.md for the reasoning and for the one term that should
still be written into the finalized Statement of Work.
